#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:3
msgid "Silicon Errata and Software Workarounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:5
msgid "Author: Will Deacon <will.deacon@arm.com>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:7
msgid "Date  : 27 November 2015"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:9
msgid ""
"It is an unfortunate fact of life that hardware is often produced with so-"
"called \"errata\", which can cause it to deviate from the architecture under "
"specific circumstances.  For hardware produced by ARM, these errata are "
"broadly classified into the following categories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:15
msgid "Category A"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:15
msgid "A critical error without a viable workaround."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:16
msgid "Category B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:16
msgid "A significant or critical error with an acceptable workaround."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:18
msgid "Category C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:18
msgid "A minor error that is not expected to occur under normal operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:22
msgid ""
"For more information, consult one of the \"Software Developers Errata "
"Notice\" documents available on infocenter.arm.com (registration required)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:26
msgid ""
"As far as Linux is concerned, Category B errata may require some special "
"treatment in the operating system. For example, avoiding a particular "
"sequence of code, or configuring the processor in a particular way. A less "
"common situation may require similar actions in order to declassify a "
"Category A erratum into a Category C erratum. These are collectively known "
"as \"software workarounds\" and are only required in the minority of cases "
"(e.g. those cases that both require a non-secure workaround *and* can be "
"triggered by Linux)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:35
msgid ""
"For software workarounds that may adversely impact systems unaffected by the "
"erratum in question, a Kconfig entry is added under \"Kernel Features\" -> "
"\"ARM errata workarounds via the alternatives framework\". With the "
"exception of workarounds for errata deemed \"rare\" by Arm, these are "
"enabled by default and patched in at runtime when an affected CPU is "
"detected. For less-intrusive workarounds, a Kconfig option is not available "
"and the code is structured (preferably with a comment) in such a way that "
"the erratum will not be hit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm64/silicon-errata.rst:44
msgid ""
"This approach can make it slightly onerous to determine exactly which errata "
"are worked around in an arbitrary kernel source tree, so this file acts as a "
"registry of software workarounds in the Linux Kernel and will be updated "
"when new workarounds are committed and backported to stable kernels."
msgstr ""

